{
  "format": "demo-disk/song",
  "version": 2,
  "name": "MIDNIGHT RUN",
  "what": "Outrun synthwave, F# minor, 130 BPM (F#m D E Bm: i VI VII iv). Shows the JUNO-106: Night Bass galloping (an eighth and two sixteenths a beat), its VCF opened and closed by commands, pumped by DUCK from the four-on-the-floor kick; sixteenth hats, the Gated Room snare, hard Syn Tom fills across the kit; Arp Saw's sixteenths from side to side into a ping-pong DELAY, Strings 80 and the PWM Pad on CHORUS II; a Saw Lead gliding by TONE PORTA, a Super Saw hook of runs into held notes with the Juno's delayed vibrato, Poly Brass doubling it an octave down; the break a Glide Lead solo, gliding, then running in sixteenths",
  "license": {
    "id": "CC0-1.0",
    "credit": "Vasily Kazantsev (PT/FM)",
    "url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
  },
